Error [E0064]: an `#FFI(c)` function body must be one string of c source
  --> tests/ui/ffi_body_not_string.jet:2:1
    |
  2 | #FFI(c) fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {
    | ^^^^^^^
 Why: the inline foreign tier carries the foreign source as a single `"""…"""` string; the Jet signature above is the checked contract (D-FFI-INLINE1)
 Fix: write the body as `{ """<c source>""" }` — one string literal, no other statements or interpolation
